first off start by removing the motherboard and unpluging any cables that are connected. remove the side panel that has the filament roll holder (remeber to unplug the cables on the buttons).
you should see a black 3d printed backplate right behind the stepper motor unplug the cables on it and remove it with the jst connector (female 4pin) solder (or crimp) the wires in the correct order with the same colour wire.
so you know what goes where then connect it to a male jst connector so you can plug it in to the new motherboard you should see the cables you unpluged earlier there should be 2 2pin jst connectors.
those are for your lights you should grab a (2pin jst female connector) and solder (or crimp) the wires in the corect order (black is ground red is pos) then conect it to your new jst header and you will have functioning lights).
you will then need to grab the nozzle holder (that is in the 3d prints folder) and connect it to the extruder area. (as shown by the included photo).
you should then grab your cable chain or if you dont have one just pull the wires to the back making sure that it can reach any part of the bed. you should then make sure that all of your connectors are in the right order for your new motherboard and you should also have a few motor drivers.
make sure they all have heatsinks as they can fail if not and plug those in you should have the new motheboard and you can instal it in the back and connect your connectors. then instal the nesesary softwear and you should be good
